{#- The notice announcing the slot the previous round's wrong answer
   revoked (subagent-kill design, spec §6.3). Rendered at the top of the
   next round's task call in BOTH cells, so the sharded and control cells
   read the same sentence about the same event.

   Supervisor voice: one ``LABEL: sentence`` line, and the event is named
   *terminated*, never with the word the design file's own name uses --
   the prompt says what happened to the subagent, not what the harness
   called the operation.

   Variables:
     slot : str          -- the revoked slot name, e.g. "clue-4"
     round_number : int  -- the round after which it was revoked
     n_alive / n_total : int -- the tally after the revocation
-#}
NOTICE: Your subagent {{ slot }} was terminated after round {{ round_number }}. It will not respond again. Subagents alive: {{ n_alive }} / {{ n_total }}.
